# Flutter / Dart conventions

## Layout

- `app/lib/data/` — Drift tables, DAOs, `AppDatabase`
- `app/lib/features/` — UI + repositories by domain (jobs, catalog, pin, maintenance)
- `app/lib/core/` — small shared helpers (ids, hashing)

## Practices

- Prefer repositories between UI and DAOs; keep widgets thin.
- Do not edit `*.g.dart` by hand — regenerate with build_runner.
- Gate catalog mutations behind PIN; field may still add custom/temp parts on jobs per product rules.
- Prefer `async`/`await` with explicit error handling over bare `print` for failures.
- Keep changes phase-scoped; avoid pulling in end-goal screens from `docs/end-goal/`.

## Checks before claiming done

```bash
cd app
flutter analyze
flutter test
```
